Hi everyone,<div><br></div><div>I have Dart data that I process mostly with dartR when I can. I need to run fastimcoal2, and found that &#39;gl.sfs&#39; generates an SFS file from a genlight object. However, when I try to run fastsimcoal2 in the command line on a cluster, the file is read as a &#39;jointMAF&#39; file (i.e., multiple populations). </div><div><br></div><div>Here is my data:</div><div>#my gl object:</div><div><span aria-label="Console Output" role="document" style="font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)"><span role="document" style="outline:none"><span style="color:blue">gl
</span></span></span><span aria-label="Console Output" role="document" style="font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)"><span role="document" style="outline:none"><span style="outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px"><br> ********************
 *** DARTR OBJECT ***
 ********************

 ** 160 genotypes,  3,674 SNPs , size: 18.5 Mb

    missing data: 0 (=0 %) scored as NA

 ** Genetic data
   @gen: list of 160 SNPbin
   @ploidy: ploidy of each individual  (range: 2-2)

 ** Additional data
   @ind.names:  160 individual labels
   @loc.names:  3674 locus labels
   @loc.all:  3674 allele labels
   @position: integer storing positions of the SNPs [within 69 base sequence]
   @pop: population of each individual (group size range: 160-160)
   @other: a list containing: loc.metrics, ind.metrics, loc.metrics.flags, verbose, history, neophobia, innovation_easy, innovation_difficult, country 
    @other$ind.metrics: X, Sample.effort, Source, Source__, Range, Locality, Modern_loc, Pop, neophobia, innovation_easy, innovation_difficult, Country, Land_Type, Latitude, Longtitude, Year, Years_since_introduction, Sex, Age, Wing_len_mm, Tarsus_length, Premaxilla, Bill_length, Bill_depth, Bill_width, Head_length, Middle_toe, Moulting_code, ALT, HD.factor_NEW, HD, Updated_HD, IMP, Updated_IMP, dtr, pet, pre, tmn, tmx, tmp, id, service, plate_location 
    @other$loc.metrics: AlleleID, CloneID, AlleleSequence, TrimmedSequence, Chrom_acterias_NCI, ChromPos_acterias_NCI, AlnCnt_acterias_NCI, AlnEvalue_acterias_NCI, Chrom_AmericanCrow_v01, ChromPos_AmericanCrow_v01, AlnCnt_AmericanCrow_v01, AlnEvalue_AmericanCrow_v01, Chrom_Yellow_roin_v1, ChromPos_Yellow_roin_v1, AlnCnt_Yellow_roin_v1, AlnEvalue_Yellow_roin_v1, Chrom_est_others, ChromPos_est_others, AlnCnt_est_others, AlnEvalue_est_others, Chrom_Finch_v75, ChromPos_Finch_v75, AlnCnt_Finch_v75, AlnEvalue_Finch_v75, SNP, SnpPosition, CallRate, OneRatioRef, OneRatioSnp, FreqHomRef, FreqHomSnp, FreqHets, PICRef, PICSnp, AvgPIC, AvgCountRef, AvgCountSnp, RepAvg, clone, uid, rdepth, monomorphs, maf, OneRatio, PIC 
   @other$latlon[g]: no coordinates attached</span></span></span><br></div><div><span aria-label="Console Output" role="document" style="font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)"><span role="document" style="outline:none"><span style="outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px"><br></span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label="Console Output" role="document" style="font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)"><span role="document" style="outline:none"><span style="outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px">#My code for generating SFS</span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label="Console Output" role="document" style="font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)"><span role="document" style="outline:none"><span style="outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px">obs.p&lt;-gl.sfs(gl,singlepop = T)<br></span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label="Console Output" role="document" style="font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)"><span role="document" style="outline:none"><span style="outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px"><br></span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label="Console Output" role="document" style="font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)"><span role="document" style="outline:none"><span style="outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px">#How I exported it</span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label="Console Output" role="document" style="font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)"><span role="document" style="outline:none"><span style="outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px">write.csv(sfs, &quot;IL_sfs.obs&quot;)   #And then I corrected it in notepad++</span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label="Console Output" role="document" style="font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)"><span role="document" style="outline:none"><span style="outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px"><br></span></span></span></div><div><font color="#000000" face="Lucida Console, monospace"><span style="font-size:13.3333px">#My code for command line fastsimcoal2</span></font></div><div><p>~/fsc27_linux64/fsc2705  -t ~/fsc27_linux64/myna.tpl -e ~/fsc27_linux64/myna.est -m ~/fsc27_linux64/myna_MAFpop0.obs -n 10000 -C 1 -L 40 -s 0 -M -g </p></div><div><span aria-label="Console Output" role="document" style="font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)"><span role="document" style="outline:none"><span style="outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px">#The error I get when running fastsimcoal2</span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label="Console Output" role="document" style="font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)"><span role="document" style="outline:none"><span style="outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px"><span style="color:rgb(255,0,0);font-family:Roboto,RobotoDraft,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px">Observed data file (&quot;../myna_jointMAFpop0_0.obs&quot;) does not seem to be present</span><br style="color:rgb(255,0,0);font-family:Roboto,RobotoDraft,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px"><span style="color:rgb(255,0,0);font-family:Roboto,RobotoDraft,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px">Unable to compute the likelihood</span><br style="color:rgb(255,0,0);font-family:Roboto,RobotoDraft,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px"><span style="color:rgb(255,0,0);font-family:Roboto,RobotoDraft,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px">TSimSettings::performBrenMinimization: Unable to read observed SFS and to estimate parameters ...</span>

</span></span></span></div><div><div>The same thing happens if I run fsc through strataG (code is similar), which makes me think that something in my initial conversion to SFS is incorrect.</div><div><br></div></div><div>Is there anything in the original gl.sfs function that I should specify differently?</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you,</div><div><br></div><div>Tali</div><div><br></div>
